"""Round 26 (the probe log): the declared changes to the Papyrus sources the historical verifiers accept. GENERATED by
build/fix26_history_gen.py from this template -- edit the reasons there, never the digests here.

Round 26 only adds logging: ESSBNative.Trace (a native that writes one [ESSB][T][pap] line into the DLL's probe log) and
the calls of it behind a level-4 check (ESSBController.Probe, LogEvent, LogThrottled, ESSBLog.Log, the handlers of the
DLL's events, 神佑, the status dump, ESSBMCM's two buttons, ESSBElem3's 以毒攻毒). No property or variable changed (the
state schema stays). The round-25 seal (build/fix25_history.py) now runs on the pre-fix26 snapshot
(.codex/pre-fix26-snapshot/src, taken before any round-26 edit), and this module proves that today's scripts differ from
that snapshot ONLY by the changes declared below, each bound to the code by digest (comment-stripped body, sha256[:16],
build/fix21_history.digest):

  CHANGED     (script, function) -> (why, before, after)
  REMOVED     (script, function) -> (why, before)
  ADDED       (script, function) -> (why, after)
  PROPERTIES  script -> (why, code lines added outside functions, code lines removed)
  FILES       whole scripts removed or added -> (why, sha256 of the file, 'removed' | 'added')

Anything else fails the build: an undeclared edit, a declared function edited after sealing, a removed script that
comes back. legacy_source() hands the older seals and verifiers the snapshot only after that proof; the chain is
fix21 -> ... -> fix25 (24 -> 25, "now" = pre-fix26) -> this one (25 -> 26, "now" = src/).
The round-26 behaviour itself is checked by build/fix26_verify.py and the native trace test.
"""
